# A full menu Grand Prix for behaviour batches (#71, Amendment 4): as gp_menu_full_press.plan, with Skip Cutscenes
# (remove) in the profile in place of the rundown press. At AI difficulty 100, run to the results screen. Tools/b0014_check.py reads the difficulty back from UDP, and any race not at 100 is invalid.
wait screen=splash 180
pad ls 15000
pad ls
pad ls 2000
pad ls
home
@sleep 3
@raw {"seq":0,"cmd":"route","args":{"route":"f1_world"},"timeout_ms":60000}
@sleep 5
@expect fe_f1_world
@raw {"seq":0,"cmd":"route","args":{"route":"play"},"timeout_ms":60000}
@sleep 6
@expect f1_world_activity_container
# the Grand Prix card
pad a 250
@sleep 6
# the season: one right is F1 2025
pad right 250
@sleep 3
pad a 250
@sleep 6
@expect solo_container
# round 1's track: ten right from Australia is Austria
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 7
@expect solo_container
# team: four right from McLaren is Aston Martin. Then the driver: Stroll is the default
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 7
@expect solo_container
pad a 250
@sleep 7
@expect settings_container
# Difficulty 100: from Start Event, right then down is the Difficulty tile. Holding right reaches the cap of 110 from
# any start, and ten presses left from there is exactly 100. Then back, and left to Start Event.
pad right 250
@sleep 2
pad down 250
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 4
pad right 6000
@sleep 2
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
@sleep 2
pad b 250
@sleep 4
# --- H-dry discovery (#118): stop here, on the settings hub with Difficulty set to 100, and take live steps from
# <Out>/control.txt (pad presses, `status`) while tools/window_frames.ps1 records the screen. Goal: find the Weather
# option and its fixed value (Clear / Dry / custom), and write down the presses. No race is started; the shell quits.
@control 900
